# Demo Patch 3 — Gitleaks: Hardcoded Secret (Critical)

## What it demonstrates
Gitleaks detects a hardcoded AWS-style access key in a source file. The
gate blocks the merge immediately.

## Trigger
Add a fake AWS key to app/main.py.

--- a/app/main.py
+++ b/app/main.py
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
 from flask import Flask, jsonify

+# DEMO ONLY — fake key, not real
+AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID = "AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE"
+AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY = "wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY"
+
 app = Flask(__name__)

## Expected gate output
Finding:     AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID = "AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE"
Secret:      AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE
RuleID:      aws-access-token
Entropy:     3.5
File:        app/main.py
Line:        3

Error: Process completed with exit code 1.

## Fix
Remove the secret. If it were real, rotate it immediately — assume it
is compromised the moment it is committed.